#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128866 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "82248f5b-84f1-5acf-ade8-4ed90a410cc3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12530" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses $m_1=1\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_2=2\\,\\textrm{kg},$ $m_3=3\\,\\textrm{kg},$ and $m_4=3\\,\\textrm{kg}$ located at $x_1=-1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_2 = 1\\,\\textrm{m},$ $x_3 = 3\\,\\textrm{m},$ and $x_4 = 5 \\, \\textrm{m},$ respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin." :question/worked-solution "The moment about the origin $O$ of a collection of masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\nM_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =1, & \\,{m}_{2} & =2, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, & \\,{m}_{4} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =1, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3, & \\,{x}_{4} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe calculate the total moment of this system about the origin as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3}+{m}_{4}{x}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-1+2+9+15 \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the total moment of the system is $25\\,\\textrm{kg} \\cdot \\textrm{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128867 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "adcc17f7-7acf-50fd-bb68-b9e6b0477fe3" :question/math-academy-id "e-12531" :question/problem "![](images/ce/cea41dc5efa961e4d0e3ccf42db21113d3b7d1d2240f3edbcc4c1f0cab61ead1.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass, denoted $\\overline{x},$ of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_n$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_O = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =2, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =3, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =2+4+3 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-2+8+12 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{x} = \\dfrac{M_O}{m} = \\dfrac{18}{9}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128868 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "0f13ad0c-9523-542d-a3bf-c562f09d6a88" :question/math-academy-id "e-12532" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0e4802c6642fc0950358235f30fb8c994d26b912e557122af08b99277bb6192a.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above. Given that the center of mass for the collection is located at $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y}),$ what is the value of $\\overline{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a collection of point masses $m_1,m_2,\\ldots,m_n$ located at $(x_1y_1),(x_2,y_2),\\ldots,(x_n,y_n)$ on the plane is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left(\\dfrac{M_y}{m},\\dfrac{M_x}{m}\\right),\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\sum\\limits_{i=1}^n m_i$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i y_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $x$-axis, and\n\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\sum_{i=1}^n m_i x_i$ is the total moment of the system about the $y$-axis.\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis.\n\nLet's denote the masses as\n\n$$\nm_1 = 3, \\qquad m_2 = 5, \\qquad m_3 = 1.\n$$\n\nThen, the corresponding $y$-coordinates of the masses are\n\n$$\ny_1 = 3, \\qquad y_2 = 0, \\qquad y_3 = 3.\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =3+5+1 \\\\  & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the moment of the system about the $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{y}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{y}_{1}+{m}_{2}{y}_{2}+{m}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3+5\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =9+0+3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{12}{9} = \\dfrac{4}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128869 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129294 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c97f4331-e2cf-5ec7-a3ea-3f03a4c60d2d" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Principle of Moments"}] :question/id #uuid "ae5cebdd-4eb8-5eed-9b89-fffb153c844b" :question/math-academy-id "e-12533" :question/problem "![](images/44/440f58e3d5e652374689083ffa672f505888259a51e1c5ef2207d94410eb8cab.png)\n\n     \n\nTwo point masses $A$ and $B$ are connected by a rigid, massless rod of length $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ that is perfectly balanced on a fulcrum, as shown above. If $B$ has mass $10\\,\\rm{lb}$ and is $4\\,\\rm{ft}$ from the fulcrum, find the mass of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $m$ be the mass of $A.$\nThe length of the rod is $9\\,\\rm{ft}$ and the distance between the fulcrum and $B$ is $4\\,\\rm{ft}.$ So, the distance between the fulcrum and $A$ is\n\n$$\n9 - 4 = 5\\,\\rm{ft},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/dc/dc2503e1ed1cd91a9f3876ec5735d5c375c36b9bcac6216659a29f5efa294ea0.png)\n\nLet's write down the moment of each mass about the fulcrum:\n\n- The moment of mass $A$ equals $-m \\cdot 5 = -5m\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (negative since the motion induced by this mass would be counterclockwise).\n\n- The moment of mass $B$ equals $10 \\cdot 4 = 40\\,\\textrm{lb}\\cdot\\textrm{ft}$ (positive since the motion induced by this mass would be clockwise).\n\nThe *principle of moments* tells us that for the two masses to balance perfectly, the sum of the moments must equal zero.\n\nTherefore, in this case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}40-5m & =0 \\\\ 5m & =40 \\\\ m & =8\\,lb.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b874ab6-331b-50ae-80f7-e72a2b840dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126732} {:answer/id #uuid "bc53e812-b31e-50ca-aa34-98b424d3d313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126733} {:answer/id #uuid "faec56ef-2a67-5c5c-bf4c-29c5f4848720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126734} {:answer/id #uuid "58c00db2-ab9b-5aef-bbc4-ee260812667e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126735} {:answer/id #uuid "72dd06d6-e6a0-518c-9320-0ff4f823a1d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126736}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2651d8cd-6740-558f-ad62-87a2259fc4f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126731}] :question/id #uuid "1371e8b7-9ee1-5f72-8099-0b1ba9daf98c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163079" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses $m_{1} = 0.5kg$, $m_{2} = 2kg$, and $m_{3} = 1kg$ located at $x_{1} = 2m$, $x_{2} = 3m$, and $x_{3} = 5m$, respectively, along the $x$-axis. Find the total moment of this system about the origin."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129291 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7ea6678-6624-5853-b137-be255a3e694e" :knowledge-point/title "Sums of Moments for Masses Distributed Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c5c0b78-81ec-5d16-93b1-2ea0e0d92ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126738} {:answer/id #uuid "9d20b7e2-f99e-54d3-929e-f31a2b35d6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126739} {:answer/id #uuid "bdca0c32-9b2d-5d00-ad69-2bd5905ab8c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126740} {:answer/id #uuid "0984b258-4bc3-5ca9-9217-2c3d9ea58224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126741} {:answer/id #uuid "592a6fad-2e82-5288-bfa4-20a66d882269" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38kg \\cdot m" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126742}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a3a538a6-239a-52ba-ad91-e6484520bb7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126737}] :question/id #uuid "9e68bef7-b75c-5baa-8bf8-48acf922e76c" :question/math-academy-id "q-163080" :question/problem "![](images/09/092a8fdc34bd72bb15f1b2ad68467232bafd5423b5662200d021eca3f249005f.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses shown above, where the distances along the $x$-axis are measured in meters. Find the total moment of this system about the origin."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129541 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129292 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9af52eb2-33a4-5655-9b1a-a07d76dc3216" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses Along the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc51275a-3238-505c-bb9d-f18fb61e4533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126744} {:answer/id #uuid "178b1a07-2916-5513-b215-0e118df04d40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126745} {:answer/id #uuid "38277cde-773b-572e-a185-e420fd7da936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126746} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac4d0b2-0351-5c6f-98ff-ee8189b1384c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{105}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126747} {:answer/id #uuid "6585fdc9-9c5f-5608-81ab-8834986c15c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126748}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a085f3cf-35c9-5534-9bdb-36dec2d80ff1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126743}] :question/id #uuid "253b036a-b515-5131-9744-15f0a018f8f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-163081" :question/problem "Consider the collection of point masses $m_{1} = 2kg$, $m_{2} = 5kg$, and $m_{3} = 7kg$ located at $x_{1} = 1.5$, $x_{2} = 5$, and $x_{3} = 10$, respectively, along the $x$-axis, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129293 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37fbfd74-981e-5281-a651-21b9ea1b7421" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Center of Mass for a Collection of Masses in the Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a840cea9-875d-5806-9749-b1cad3c12497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{12}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126756} {:answer/id #uuid "03f4681f-e4aa-5573-8bfc-d6735a168c93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126757} {:answer/id #uuid "0e05d6e9-5f4b-5d3e-b3e2-e0c53b441921" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126758} {:answer/id #uuid "3399dbf2-0d3b-5140-b468-f8c7977c9def" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{18}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126759} {:answer/id #uuid "39da1e78-3bd7-5538-9c64-88552580b68f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126760}] :answer-field/id #uuid "cec1597b-145a-5f80-bebd-a8347c83ce22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/i